 ## [Unreleased]
 
+## [0.8.2] - 2026-11-19
+
+### Security
+- GHSA-m9mq-7m7q-xc6p: fixed an arbitrary file write. `browser_download`'s `save_dir` is now confined under the download root (`~/.browse-mcp/downloads`), and `browser_save_state` / `browser_load_state`'s explicit `path` is confined under `~/.browse-mcp/state`. Absolute paths and `..` escapes are rejected, and download filenames are reduced to a bare basename. Both data roots can still be moved with `BROWSE_MCP_HOME`.
+- The `force_fetch` fallback in `browser_download` now applies the `BROWSE_MCP_ALLOWED_ORIGINS` / `BROWSE_MCP_BLOCKED_ORIGINS` origin fence to the initial URL and to every redirect hop. Before, it used a raw `fetch()` that skipped the fence.
+
 ## [0.8.1] - 2026-06-12
 
 ### Added
